  "notes": "{訴|うった}える is an ichidan verb with two main meanings: to sue (legal) and to appeal/complain (emotional).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n\nPARTICLE PATTERNS:\n- Xを{訴|うった}える: to complain about X, to sue over X\n- Xに{訴|うった}える: to appeal to X (person/court)\n- Xを{相手|あいて}に{訴|うった}える: to sue X (defendant)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {裁判|さいばん}に{訴|うった}える: to take to court\n- {感情|かんじょう}に{訴|うった}える: to appeal to emotions\n- {痛|いた}みを{訴|うった}える: to complain of pain\n- {無実|むじつ}を{訴|うった}える: to plead innocence\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {訴|うった}え: appeal, complaint (noun)\n- {訴訟|そしょう}: lawsuit\n- {告訴|こくそ}する: to file a criminal complaint\n- {起訴|きそ}する: to prosecute, to indict",
